Hi Miguel,

To answer your specific questions about the initial values, if you specify initial values for tau.sq.beta with fix = FALSE, it will use those initial values for tau.sq.beta for the first chain, then it will draw realistic random values from the priors for the additional chains (if you run more than one). There is not a way to randomize all initial values except for tau.sq.beta (or any other parameter).

I would not expect the initial values for tau.sq.beta to really aid in convergence much at all. The fact that the model sometimes converges and sometimes does not converge indicates to me that you have likely overfit the model and are trying to estimate too many parameters given the data set you're working with. So, my recommendation would be to simplify the model until you see more stable convergence.

Jeff

